she stormed out.

264
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:55,980
Which was sad, because we were playing Scrabble,

265
00:11:55,980 --> 00:12:00,050
and I had all the letters to spell "persimmon."

266
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:05,830
Why are you even part of this conversation?

267
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:07,690
You don't know anything about women.

268
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:10,360
I know that if I had a wife or a fiance,

269
00:12:10,370 --> 00:12:12,400
I'd ask her first before I invested money

270
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,490
in a comic book store.

271
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:16,650
He's right.

272
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:18,250
Yeah, well, of course I am.

273
00:12:18,250 --> 00:12:19,800
I was also right about her hair.

274
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,910
It did everything but quack.

275
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:27,250
There's something I wanted to run past you.

276
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:28,340
What's up?

277
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:30,230
Mm, the guys and I were thinking about

278
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:32,220
investing in Stuart's comic book store.

279
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:34,690
- Is that okay? - Why are you asking me?

280
00:12:34,690 --> 00:12:36,520
Well, you know, we're engaged,

281
00:12:36,530 --> 00:12:39,030
and it's kind of a big deal financially.

282
00:12:39,030 --> 00:12:41,330
It seems like something we should talk about.

283
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,000
Well, would you consider mounds of credit card debt

284
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,600
kind of a big deal financially?

285
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:50,800
Yeah.

286
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:58,160
So, me and the guys were talking about

287
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:00,410
this great investment opportunity...

288
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:01,250
Nope.

289
00:13:03,570 --> 00:13:05,180
But you didn't hear what it was.

290
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,440
I know.

291
00:13:09,370 --> 00:13:10,850
Oh, come on.

292
00:13:10,850 --> 00:13:12,050
Fine. What is it?

293
00:13:12,050 --> 00:13:14,360
It's to help reopen the comic book store.

294
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,980
Nope.

295
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:18,160
Well, hear me out.

296
00:13:18,170 --> 00:13:20,330
Howard, you know we're saving up for a house.

297
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:22,290
I know, but all the guys are doing it.

298
00:13:22,290 --> 00:13:23,660
We're splitting it four ways,

299
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:25,930
so it's really not that much money.

300
00:13:26,370 --> 00:13:28,600
It just seems like a risky investment.

301
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:31,020
I get that. I...

302
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:34,910
Okay, look...

303
00:13:36,370 --> 00:13:40,920
The reason this is important is...

304
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:45,690
...before my dad left me and my mom...

305
00:13:45,690 --> 00:13:50,300
he used to... take me to the comic book store.

306
00:13:50,510 --> 00:13:54,130
It was one of the few things we did together.

307
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:57,460
Oh. Howie, I had no idea.

308
00:13:57,460 --> 00:14:00,630
Well, I don't... like to talk about it.

309
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:03,400
Oh, baby.

310
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:06,500
That story's made up, isn't it?

311
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:12,200
That's how much buying a comic book store means to me.

312
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:16,860
I'd like your honest opinion on something.

313
00:14:17,410 --> 00:14:18,780
Of course.

314
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:20,490
Now, before I start,

315
00:14:20,490 --> 00:14:23,900
I need you to know that I'm very excited about this,

316
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:26,130
and anything you say

317
00:14:26,130 --> 00:14:28,190
that isn't enthusiastically supportive

318
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:32,770
will throw our entire relationship into question.

319
00:14:34,430 --> 00:14:35,800
So...

320
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:38,440
keep an open mind.

321
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:41,790
I'm feeling a little backed into a corner, Sheldon.

322
00:14:41,790 --> 00:14:44,100
Perfect. Now...

323
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:47,310
...I'm considering investing

324
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:50,150
in Stuart's comic book store.

325
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:52,770
Interesting.

326
00:14:54,650 --> 00:14:57,150
Can you see how a grown man,

327
00:14:57,150 --> 00:14:59,260
an accomplished scientist,

328
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:01,180
who invests in a store

329
00:15:01,180 --> 00:15:03,320
that sells picture books

330
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:06,810
about flying men in colorful underwear...

331
00:15:07,710 --> 00:15:10,140
...might be wasting both his financial

332
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:12,860
and intellectual resources?

333
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:20,280
No.

334
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:25,150
Then I think it's a terrific idea.

335
00:15:25,930 --> 00:15:27,040
Great.

336
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:30,520
Wait till you hear about our van.

337
00:15:36,190 --> 00:15:37,380
Thanks for inviting us over.

338
00:15:37,380 --> 00:15:38,750
Oh, thank you for coming.

339
00:15:38,750 --> 00:15:41,160
Uh, listen, Penny, before you start,

340
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:43,220
I just want to apologize for being so rude

341
00:15:43,220 --> 00:15:44,380
the other day in my office.

342
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:45,890
No, no. No need to apologize.

343
00:15:45,890 --> 00:15:47,680
Excuse me, can I say something?

344
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,300
I just love both you guys,

345
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:52,060
and I want you to get along.

346
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:54,490
And when I say "love," I meant as a friend.

347
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:58,780
And, uh, way too soon, right?

348
00:15:59,630 --> 00:16:01,330
Okay, sit down. Listen, Emily,

349
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:02,860
what happened between me and Raj

350
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:04,490
- was a long time ago. - It was,

351
00:16:04,490 --> 00:16:07,000
and I may have made it seem like a bigger deal than I should have.

352
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,580
Yeah, and Leonard and I are engaged now,

353
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:11,460
and I'm just hoping we can put this whole thing behind us.

354
00:16:11,850 --> 00:16:13,290
I'd like that, too.

355
00:16:13,290 --> 00:16:15,150
Yeah, I thought I'd be okay with it,

356
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:17,160
but then I saw how pretty you are.

357
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:19,000
Oh, that's so sweet.

358
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,060
I mean, look at you-- you are gorgeous.

359
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:23,840
It's true-- you're both gorgeous.

360
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:28,330
Kind of says something about the man who could bed you both.

361
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:38,290
You get why I've been alone most of my adult life.

362
00:16:40,780 --> 00:16:42,780
So, what brings you by?

363
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:45,990
Well, I don't need a reason-- it's my house.

364
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,380
Technically, it's your mom's house, but...

365
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:51,580
we certainly want you to feel welcome.

366
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:54,170
I'm always welcome.

367
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:57,590
Mm, just... try and call first.

368
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,980
Okay, let's get down to business.

369
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,910
Howie was thinking about putting up some money

370
00:17:02,910 --> 00:17:04,360
to help you reopen the store,

371
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:07,290
but before that happens, I have a few questions.

372
00:17:07,850 --> 00:17:08,990
I appreciate the offer,

373
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:12,320
but actually your mother already gave me the money.

374
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:15,350
What?

375
00:17:16,830 --> 00:17:18,540
Yeah. I told her it was too much,

376
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:21,870
but she said she was happy to help out her bubala.

377
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:25,280
Excuse me.

378
00:17:26,030 --> 00:17:28,510
Ma, you are canceling that check,

379
00:17:28,510 --> 00:17:31,200
and Stuart is not your bubala; I'm your bubala.

380
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,770
You can't have more than one bubala!

381
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:35,930
I don't know who he's talking to.

382
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:38,740
She's at Target, buying me shirts.

383
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:44,280
I'm so glad we could work this all out.

384
00:17:44,280 --> 00:17:46,080
Yeah, me, too.

385
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:48,010
You know, we should have dinner one night with you and Leonard.

386
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:49,290
Oh, we would love that.

387
00:17:49,290 --> 00:17:50,080
Great!

388
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:53,340
- Okay, good night, guys. - All right, night.

389
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:54,840
Bye.

390
00:17:55,490 --> 00:17:57,620
- I hate her. - I hate her.

391
00:18:02,690 --> 00:18:03,930
I'm really disappointed we're not gonna have

392
00:18:03,930 --> 00:18:05,880
- our own comic book store. - I know.

393
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,080
I was looking forward to it.

394
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:10,080
It would've been so nice to have a place that was ours,

395
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:13,000
where we could just sit and read comics in peace.

396
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,320
With comfy seats.

397
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:15,700
And snacks.

398
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:17,940
Well, I guess it was too good to be true.

399
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:19,430
Yeah.

